#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""p5.py - Phase 5 holdout tooling (staged 2026-10-29 in staging/phase5). Nothing here calls the model, LDR, the
proxy or SearXNG and nothing uses the GPU: it reads the config, question files, run folders and (tally only, after
every grade is written) the blind keys and the frozen answers for the string cross-check.

  plan [--out PATH] [--allow-placeholder]
        the queue plan (bench2-queue.sh / bench2.py format) for both arms from p5.json; refuses PLACEHOLDER values and
        items the queue cannot switch
  check-engine      the server on 8080 (if up) and the promoted config (what strata-ensure.sh starts on demand) must
                    both be p5.json's engine.config, with sha256(exe)[:12] = engine.sha12
  check-frozen      every sha256 line of the FROZEN-*.txt files the holdout uses still matches
  swap-mark         remember /proc/vmstat's swap counters (p5-start.sh, at the start); `status` prints the change
  status            per arm and set: done / failed / not yet, wall time so far, swap since swap-mark
  packets [--out DIR] [--allow-missing] [--force]
        blind packets. checkable/<id>/question.md + A.md, B.md: each run's Answer section ("## Answer", else "## Key
        findings", else the report's lead before its sources), cleaned by tools/blind-open.py's clean() (title, inline
        check marks, setup-check notes, dropped sections), then citations, links and heading marks taken out; labels in
        a random order per question; checkable/KEY-do-not-open-before-grading.json; MANIFEST.json (no setup names);
        grader-<batch>.md per batch. open/<id>/A.md, B.md through tools/blind-open.py (BLIND_OUT=<out>/open,
        BLIND_DROP from p5.json) + open/grader-<id>.md
  tally [--out DIR] [--partial]
        refuses until every packet has a grade (checkable/grades/<id>.json, open/grades-<id>.json); then opens the keys
        and writes REPORT.md + p5-results.json: the checkable (25) line, the harder line (each of the four per setup),
        correct / wrong commitment / hedged / non-answer in their own columns, the open questions' totals, the string
        cross-check, engine and wall time per run

--config PATH (default: p5.json next to this file) works for every command; the tests use their own.
"""
